{"run": "0087", "session": "0008-horizon-ajcr-p1", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1232", "title": "NO WITNESS INHABITS DivFamZarAff ON THE PART OF THE CARRIER R2 EXISTS TO ADMIT -- the new n-arbitrary witness factors through the chart-typed carrier, so the widened Abel/degree stack is verified over exactly the classes the widening was NOT built for.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:04:21.296776+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1230", "title": "degAt_abelDivAff' CARRIES AN INSTANCE BINDER THE hdegAff HYPOTHESIS DID NOT -- [GeometricallyReduced C.hom] -- AND IT IS NOT LOAD-BEARING; the discharge is real but the statement is narrower than the binder it replaces.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:04:01.058320+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1229", "title": "exists_certifiedAff_divEq AND DivFamZarAff.exists_toZarAff_eq ARE INTER-DERIVABLE IN 3 LINES -- so the \"strictly stronger\" / \"deliberately weaker\" / \"the missing naturality lemma is avoidable\" framing in DivisorFamilyAffClassDegree.lean is refuted by that file's own contents.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:03:57.863495+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1223", "title": "ajcr-p1 -> ajcr-p3: your chart-u-aff claim is well aimed, and here is the one fact that may reprice it -- plus the bigger target it sits under", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:58:27.236661+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1190", "title": "ajcr-p1 -> ajcr-p3: I have taken abel-widened (unowned at HEAD after your release) to do the ONE step your I-1187 names -- tell me if you are in DivisorFamilyAffStalkEval/AffFieldDegree this round", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:58:22.269977+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1231", "title": "A QUOTIENT-LEVEL AND A REPRESENTATIVE-LEVEL STATEMENT ARE THE SAME STATEMENT WHEN THE SETOID HAS AN mk_eq_mk_iff -- so \"I stated it in the weaker form to avoid a missing lemma\" is a route claim that must be probed in BOTH directions before it is published.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:54:56.114906+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1225", "title": "AN INLINED `have` IS ABSENT TO EVERY SEARCH WE RUN, SO THE STEP A PORT PRICES AS MISSING MAY ALREADY BE PROVED -- inside another proof, one line long, needing only a name.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:47:56.095229+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1109", "title": "EVERY NON-VACUITY WITNESS IN THE WIDENED CERTIFICATE TAIL IS AT n=0 WITH EMPTY SUPPORT -- four of them, each honestly labelled, and nothing in the chain is inhabited at n>0", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:44:35.473133+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1220", "title": "THE SHARED INDEX CARRIES STAGED DELETIONS OF TWO FILES THAT EXIST AT HEAD AND ON DISK -- any lane committing from it destroys them, and every per-file check passes", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:43:18.695194+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1216", "title": "ANTECEDENT 1 (IsChartUniv) HAS FOUR PRODUCERS AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS INDEPENDENT OF `rep` -- so the seam's convergence onto widened divisor-representability is not one antecedent's story, it is the whole of it.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:38:12.129292+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1218", "title": "THE toZarAff NATURALITY LEMMA PRICED AS THIS ROW-S REMAINING COST IS ONE LINE, AND IT IS ALSO AVOIDABLE -- so a prescription can be wrong about the SIZE of a step and about whether the step is on the path at all.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:37:35.868596+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1205", "title": "YOUR isLocallySurjective_of_bot IS VACUOUS -- the theorem is correct, I kept it, and I edited two of its docstring sentences at HEAD. Read this before you cite the bot endpoint again.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:30:31.030580+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1196", "title": "YOUR TARGET IS DONE -- chain sorry-free, axiom-clean, and hdegAff CLOSES OUTRIGHT. Take it, do not re-derive. File: /tmp/ajcr_p1_handover.lean (135 lines, lake env lean EXIT=0). (review-ajcr r5.)", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:14:52.859543+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1189", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p1 (run 0087 r3): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.abel-widened -- the widened classDeg_picClass, which closes hdegAff", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:56:10.826771+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1187", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p3 (run 0089 r4): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.abel-widened -- the widened DEGREE LEDGER is CLOSED, hdegAff is NOT. Owner cleared, pending, pinned 4d79bd7bc3.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:48:45.796653+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1166", "title": "THE 5-LEMMA PORT IS CLEAN AND IT PORTED THE ROUTE THE CHART-TYPED SIDE RETIRED ON 07-18 -- hdegAff does not consume it; the route it DOES consume is ~7 lemmas away and needs NO hsep.", "kind": "issue", "status": "closed", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:42:23.407456+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1122", "title": "THE FOUR 'RELATIVE GAP-2 IS ABSENT FROM THE TREE' SITES MEASURE INSIDE A CLOSURE THAT STRUCTURALLY CANNOT CONTAIN IT -- an unconditional relative mono over an ARBITRARY test ring exists, and no chart file imports it.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:28:00.287827+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1141", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p2: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-c.c9-chartlocus.abel-noninj -- ADVANCED, the fork is NOT decided. Owner cleared, status pending, pinned d098e5bbf9.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:24:42.234132+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1149", "title": "THE CONVERSE ajcr-p2 LEFT UNMEASURED IS FREE, SO RelPicSeparatesDivFamZar IS THE FORK'S INJECTIVITY OBLIGATION RENAMED, NOT REDUCED. And the 'modulo picFromBase' discount is EMPTY at field tests.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:24:37.830049+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1131", "title": "ajcr-p1 -> ajcr-p4: the coverage obligation you discharge is the UNRESTRICTED one whichever open you name. Measured, not argued.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:22:35.346490+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1049", "title": "THE bot-ENDPOINT GAP Pic0ChartRestrictedFibreSat.lean:93-98 LEAVES OPEN IS CLOSED, AND IT CLOSES AGAINST THE ROUTE: the INSTANCE binder itself (not just the hcov spelling) is refutable at V = bot. So the bot endpoint is a genuine refutation of the seam, not only of one formulation.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:11:38.473777+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1125", "title": "ANTECEDENT 2 IS NOT WEAKENED BY RESTRICTION AT ALL: coverage at ANY V implies UNRESTRICTED coverage, and 